course: dictionary
lesson: 14605
title: A long word with a short name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Poliomyelitis is a very long word, but you can use its short name, polio. Doctors and families often say polio, and both words mean the same illness.
explain: Polio is a serious disease caused by a virus, which is a tiny germ. The virus attacks the nerves, and this can paralyse a person, so their muscles stop working and they cannot move that part of their body. «The vaccine protects children from polio.» The word vaccine is the clue: it is a medicine that stops you catching the illness.
explain: When you meet a new word, swap your meaning into the sentence. Try «The medicine protects children from a serious illness.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is probably right.
fact: Poliomyelitis is the full name of polio.
fact: Polio is a serious disease caused by a virus.
fact: Polio can paralyse people, especially children, which means their muscles stop working.
fact: A vaccine can prevent polio.
fact: Thanks to vaccines, polio is now very rare in the world.
exercise: «The vaccine protects children from polio.» What does a vaccine do? | *It stops you catching a serious illness like polio | It makes you sleepy for a week | It makes you taller
exercise: Polio is caused by what? | *A virus, a tiny germ | Eating too many sweets | Cold wind
exercise: Polio is the short name for which long word? | *Poliomyelitis | Politics | Pollution
test: «Polio can paralyse a child's legs.» What does paralyse mean here? | Make them run very fast | *Stop the muscles working so they cannot move | Make them grow longer
test: Which of these can prevent polio? | *A vaccine | Staying up late | Eating crisps
exam: What is poliomyelitis? | *A serious disease caused by a virus that can paralyse people | A famous doctor | A type of bird | A kind of sweet
